    Bug 2047084 - Factor out duplicated S/MIME self-cert verification in nsMsgComposeSecure. r=kaie

    MimeCryptoHackCerts verified the sender's own encryption and signing
    certificates with two near-identical blocks, each mapping a
    verification failure to a human-readable NSS reason.

    Factor the shared logic into two file-static helpers, VerifySelfCert
    and GetCertVerificationErrorReason. The FindCertByDBKey lookup and its
    result handling stay inline in each path, so the surrounding control
    flow and the returned nsresult are unchanged.

    No behavior change.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309752

